tottf: Fix hmtx table (all widths zero) for monospaced fonts

Upstream: https://github.com/fontforge/fontforge/pull/5702 (merged
2025-12-08, after the 20251009 release).

Since #5506 (in 20251009) SFComputePitch ignores zero-width glyphs when
deciding whether a font is fixed pitch, so a monospace font whose marks
have zero advance is still "fixed pitch". dumpglyphs then writes only
the first four long hmtx metrics (lasthwidth = 3), which silently gives
every later glyph the fourth glyph's advance: zero-width marks in such a
font come out one cell wide (culmus's Miriam Mono CLM faces; FreeMono on
its next rebuild). Fonts whose inputs have no zero-width glyphs (DejaVu
Sans Mono, Mitra Mono, Symbols Nerd Font Mono) are not affected. Drop
the lasthwidth shortcut, as upstream did.

--- a/fontforge/tottf.c
+++ b/fontforge/tottf.c
@@ -1459,7 +1459,6 @@ static int dumpglyphs(SplineFont *sf,struct glyphinfo *gi) {
     FigureFullMetricsEnd(sf,gi,true);
 
     if ( fixed>0 ) {
-	gi->lasthwidth = 3;
 	gi->hfullcnt = 3;
     }
     for ( i=0; i<gi->gcnt; ++i ) {
